          "type": "turn",
          "question": "Is there a questionnaire they use for it?",
          "answer": "Yes, for Generalized Anxiety Disorder (GAD), the seven-item Generalized Anxiety Disorder questionnaire is commonly used. This questionnaire helps to screen for GAD and track how severe it is. Scores on this questionnaire are often categorized into severity bands: 5 for mild, 10 for moderate, and 15 for severe. A score of 10 or more usually leads to further assessment. (Source: Generalized anxiety disorder: screening instruments and first-line care)\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
